package: @astryxdesign/lab

# ListInput

Use for compact ordered records: fewer than 7 items and up to 3 simple consistent fields. Add/remove motion does not delay onChange or focus and becomes instant under reduced motion. Use Table or a dedicated flow for larger or complex data.

**Import:** `import {ListInput} from '@astryxdesign/lab';`

## Anatomy

| Element | Required | Description |
|---------|----------|-------------|
| Label and description | Yes | Names the complete collection and optionally explains what records to add. |
| First-record field labels | Yes | ListInput renders primary-tone column labels without separate table chrome and keeps each rendered control's own label visually hidden but semantically associated. At wider widths, repeated labels are visually hidden; when fields stack at 640px or narrower, every record shows its field labels. |
| Record fields | Yes | Consumer-rendered inputs that receive scoped record state, complete validation status, the native tooltip status variant, and update behavior. When stacked responsively, label-to-input spacing is smallest, field spacing is larger, and record groups use 32px separation so each object remains visually distinct. |
| Remove action | Yes | Removes its record immediately, moves focus to a predictable neighboring control, and animates surviving rows into their new positions when supported. It is revealed while the record is hovered or contains keyboard focus and stays visible on touch screens; at rest it is transparent but keeps its column and its place in the tab order, so the fields never shift. In the stacked layout, it aligns beside the first field at the top of the record. |
| Reorder handle | No | Core List's reorder handle, three lines at the end of the record after Remove, in Remove's cell, with an accessible label naming the record and its position and no hover tooltip. Where the primary pointer is coarse, its target grows to at least 44 by 44 px. It is revealed while the record is hovered or contains keyboard focus and stays visible on touch screens; at rest it is transparent but stays in the tab order. In the stacked layout it sits at the top of the record beside Remove. A finger holds it a moment, then drags; a mouse drags at once; activating it (Space or Enter) turns on reorder mode, where Arrow Up and Arrow Down move the record a place and Escape ends the mode. |
| Reorder-mode hint | No | While a record is in reorder mode, core List's hint anchored to its handle shows the moves and Done as buttons, so taps alone can reorder. Each does what its key does and leaves the focus on the handle. |
| Empty state | No | When no records exist, a centered compact EmptyState names the empty collection and directs users to the Add action. |
| Add action | Yes | Fills the record-fields width, uses the inherited medium control size shared by ListInput fields and actions, and immediately appends a new record created by createItem unless maxItems has been reached. On pointer activation, available vertical scroll containers offset the inserted height from nearest to outermost so the action remains under the pointer; keyboard activation keeps the normal focus behavior, and newly focused field visibility always wins. The live row uses tokenized translate entrance motion when supported, and focus moves to its first field without waiting for the animation. |
| Validation messages | No | Explain field-, item-, or list-level errors, warnings, and success states. Field messages use each input's native tooltip status affordance and do not change row height. Item messages align to the record fields without extending under the remove control. |

## Best Practices

- **Do:** Use stable keys and consistent columns.
- **Do:** Validate at field, item, or list scope as appropriate.
- **Do:** Reorder through the handle; one onReorder call per drop or key move, and no onChange; focus stays on the handle.
- **Do:** Keep add/remove motion non-blocking and instant under reduced motion.
- **Don't:** Use for long datasets or complex/inconsistent records.
- **Don't:** Block removal to enforce a minimum; report a list error instead.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `label` | `string` | - | Collection label and accessible name. **(required)** |
| `value` | `T[]` | - | Controlled ordered records. **(required)** |
| `onChange` | `(next: T[], change: ListInputChange<T>) => void` | - | Emits next records plus add/update/remove metadata. **(required)** |
| `getItemKey` | `(item: T) => React.Key` | - | Required stable unique record identity. **(required)** |
| `createItem` | `() => T` | - | Creates a new keyed record for Add. **(required)** |
| `columns` | `ListInputColumn<T>[]` | - | Typed simple fields: key, header, optional proportional/pixel width, and renderInput. ListInput owns visible column labels; narrow records stack with repeated labels, stronger separation, and top-aligned row actions. Renderers forward status and statusVariant. **(required)** |
| `itemName` | `string` | - | Singular noun for actions and announcements. |
| `description` | `string` | - | Supporting text below the label. |
| `status` | `InputStatus` | - | List-level InputStatus. |
| `getItemStatus` | `(item: T, index: number) => InputStatus \| undefined` | - | Per-record InputStatus resolver. |
| `getFieldStatus` | `(item: T, columnKey: string, index: number) => InputStatus \| undefined` | - | Per-field resolver; complete status plus tooltip variant are forwarded to the rendered input. |
| `reorderable` | `Reorderable` | - | createReorderable object keyed by getItemKey: core List's reorder handle at each record's end (after Remove), revealed on hover/focus, shown on touch: hold then drag (touch), drag (mouse), activate for reorder mode then arrows (keys), with a hint showing the moves and Done; the record dims while a copy follows and a line marks the drop, the other records stay still; each move goes to the object's onReorder({key, to}); its isReorderable keeps a record in place; handles stay focusable but inert while disabled or loading. |
| `isDisabled` | `boolean` | `false` | Disables collection, actions, and rendered inputs. |
| `isLoading` | `boolean` | `false` | Marks busy and prevents changes. |
| `maxItems` | `number` | - | Makes Add unavailable at the limit. |
| `isLabelHidden` | `boolean` | `false` | Visually hides label only. |
| `isOptional` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows Optional; exclusive with isRequired. |
| `isRequired` | `boolean` | `false` | Shows Required + accessible requirement; exclusive with isOptional. |

## Examples

### Tag options

```tsx
import {createReorderable} from '@astryxdesign/core';
import {Selector} from '@astryxdesign/core/Selector';
import {proportional} from '@astryxdesign/core/Table';
import {TextInput} from '@astryxdesign/core/TextInput';

type TagOption = {id: string; color: string; label: string};

const columns = [
  {
    key: 'color',
    header: 'Color',
    width: proportional(1, {minWidth: 120}),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, updateItem}) => (
      <Selector
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        options={colorOptions}
        value={item.color}
        onChange={color => updateItem({...item, color}, 'color')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
      />
    ),
  },
  {
    key: 'label',
    header: 'Label',
    width: proportional(2, {minWidth: 200}),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, updateItem}) => (
      <TextInput
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        value={item.label}
        onChange={nextLabel => updateItem({...item, label: nextLabel}, 'label')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
      />
    ),
  },
] satisfies ListInputColumn<TagOption>[];

// Each move lands where ListInput reports it: the record's key and index.
const reorderable = useMemo(
  () =>
    createReorderable({
      onReorder: ({key, to}) =>
        setTags(tags => {
          const rest = tags.filter(tag => tag.id !== key);
          return [...rest.slice(0, to), ...tags.filter(tag => tag.id === key), ...rest.slice(to)];
        }),
    }),
  [],
);

<ListInput
  label="Tag options"
  itemName="tag"
  value={tags}
  onChange={setTags}
  getItemKey={tag => tag.id}
  createItem={() => ({id: crypto.randomUUID(), color: 'blue', label: ''})}
  columns={columns}
  reorderable={reorderable}
  status={
    tags.length < 5
      ? {type: 'error', message: 'Add at least five tag options.'}
      : undefined
  }
  getItemStatus={tag =>
    tag.color === 'green' && tag.label === 'Blocked'
      ? {type: 'error', message: '"Blocked" cannot use green.'}
      : undefined
  }
/>
```

### Controlled guest list

```tsx
import {createReorderable} from '@astryxdesign/core';
import {proportional} from '@astryxdesign/core/Table';

type Guest = {id: string; name: string; email: string};

const columns = [
  {
    key: 'name',
    header: 'Name',
    width: proportional(1),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, isLoading, updateItem}) => (
      <TextInput
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        value={item.name}
        onChange={name => updateItem({...item, name}, 'name')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
        isLoading={isLoading}
      />
    ),
  },
  {
    key: 'email',
    header: 'Email',
    width: proportional(2),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, isLoading, updateItem}) => (
      <TextInput
        type="email"
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        value={item.email}
        onChange={email => updateItem({...item, email}, 'email')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
        isLoading={isLoading}
      />
    ),
  },
] satisfies ListInputColumn<Guest>[];

// Each move lands where ListInput reports it: the record's key and index.
const reorderable = useMemo(
  () =>
    createReorderable({
      onReorder: ({key, to}) =>
        setGuests(guests => {
          const rest = guests.filter(guest => guest.id !== key);
          return [...rest.slice(0, to), ...guests.filter(guest => guest.id === key), ...rest.slice(to)];
        }),
    }),
  [],
);

<ListInput
  label="Guests"
  itemName="guest"
  value={guests}
  onChange={setGuests}
  getItemKey={guest => guest.id}
  createItem={() => ({id: crypto.randomUUID(), name: '', email: ''})}
  columns={columns}
  reorderable={reorderable}
  maxItems={6}
  getFieldStatus={(guest, key) =>
    key === 'email' && guest.email === ''
      ? {type: 'error', message: 'Enter an email address'}
      : undefined
  }
  status={
    guests.length === 0
      ? {type: 'error', message: 'Add at least one guest'}
      : undefined
  }
/>
```

### Mailing list

```tsx
import {TextInput} from '@astryxdesign/core/TextInput';

type Subscriber = {id: string; email: string};

<ListInput
  label="Mailing list"
  itemName="subscriber"
  value={subscribers}
  onChange={setSubscribers}
  getItemKey={subscriber => subscriber.id}
  createItem={() => ({id: crypto.randomUUID(), email: ''})}
  columns={[
    {
      key: 'email',
      header: 'Email address',
      renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, updateItem}) => (
        <TextInput
          type="email"
          label={label}
          isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
          value={item.email}
          onChange={email => updateItem({...item, email}, 'email')}
          status={status}
          statusVariant={statusVariant}
          isDisabled={isDisabled}
        />
      ),
    },
  ] satisfies ListInputColumn<Subscriber>[]}
  isRequired
  maxItems={6}
  getItemStatus={subscriber =>
    isDuplicateAddress(subscriber)
      ? {type: 'error', message: 'This address is already in the list.'}
      : undefined
  }
/>
```

### Budget allocation

```tsx
import {NumberInput} from '@astryxdesign/core/NumberInput';
import {Selector} from '@astryxdesign/core/Selector';
import {pixel, proportional} from '@astryxdesign/core/Table';

type Allocation = {id: string; team: string; percent: number | null};

const columns = [
  {
    key: 'team',
    header: 'Team',
    width: proportional(2, {minWidth: 180}),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, updateItem}) => (
      <Selector
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        options={teamOptions}
        value={item.team}
        placeholder="Choose a team"
        onChange={team => updateItem({...item, team}, 'team')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
      />
    ),
  },
  {
    key: 'percent',
    header: 'Allocation',
    width: pixel(132),
    renderInput: ({item, label, isLabelHidden, status, statusVariant, isDisabled, updateItem}) => (
      <NumberInput
        label={label}
        isLabelHidden={isLabelHidden}
        value={item.percent}
        onChange={percent => updateItem({...item, percent}, 'percent')}
        status={status}
        statusVariant={statusVariant}
        isDisabled={isDisabled}
        min={0}
        max={100}
        units="%"
        isIntegerOnly
      />
    ),
  },
] satisfies ListInputColumn<Allocation>[];

<ListInput
  label="Quarterly budget allocation"
  itemName="allocation"
  value={allocations}
  onChange={setAllocations}
  getItemKey={allocation => allocation.id}
  createItem={() => ({id: crypto.randomUUID(), team: '', percent: null})}
  columns={columns}
  maxItems={4}
  status={
    total === 100
      ? undefined
      : {type: 'error', message: 'Allocations must total 100%.'}
  }
/>
```

### Family member declaration

```tsx
import {DateInput} from '@astryxdesign/core/DateInput';
import {Selector} from '@astryxdesign/core/Selector';
